FFmpeg license text for macOS installs

The Martin Riedl macOS FFmpeg zip contains only the ffmpeg binary, so
install-ffmpeg.js copies this file to vendor/ffmpeg/LICENSE when the
darwin pin has no licenseInArchive.

General FFmpeg licensing information:
  https://ffmpeg.org/legal.html

LICENSE.txt is the GNU General Public License v3 text shipped in the
BtbN FFmpeg-Builds linux archive pinned in scripts/ffmpeg-hashes.json
(autobuild-2026-07-31-14-10 / ffmpeg-n7.1.5-12-g1fdbca85aa-linux64-gpl-7.1/LICENSE.txt).
It is FFmpeg's license text from that build, not terms invented for Tessel.
